(64466, 1819, 1569, '<td valign="top">The figures in the foreground are too distracting.</td>', 'The figures in the foreground are too distracting.', '2002-05-27 14:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64467, 1819, 327, '<td valign="top">Exellent title, fun shot and it''s _people_! <br/>Would of liked the top cropped a tad and the over all shot is too dark. Good work.</td>', 'Exellent title, fun shot and it''s _people_! Would of liked the top cropped a tad and the over all shot is too dark. Good work.', '2002-05-27 16:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64468, 1819, 1540, '<td valign="top">If this photo was cropped to take out the peorple up front it would have been one of my tops pics... good shot though.</td>', 'If this photo was cropped to take out the peorple up front it would have been one of my tops pics... good shot though.', '2002-05-27 18:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64469, 1819, 1061, '<td valign="top">Good!</td>', 'Good!', '2002-05-27 21:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64470, 1819, 741, '<td valign="top">This would have been even better without the foreground.  I know the rules don''t allow it, but this would really suit a panaoramic style wide format.</td>', 'This would have been even better without the foreground.  I know the rules don''t allow it, but this would really suit a panaoramic style wide format.', '2002-05-28 01:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64471, 1819, 656, '<td valign="top">this would make a really strong silohette.  Not sure I like the people in the foreground, maybe you could have framed it higher ?</td>', 'this would make a really strong silohette.  Not sure I like the people in the foreground, maybe you could have framed it higher ?', '2002-05-28 13:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64472, 1819, 1005, '<td valign="top">If this is an afternoon shot, it needed to be a morning shot, or vise versa.  Boys appear almost as shadows.  Foreground too distracting/busy.<br/>Photo 8 Creativity 8 People 9 total 8</td>', 'If this is an afternoon shot, it needed to be a morning shot, or vise versa.  Boys appear almost as shadows.  Foreground too distracting/busy.Photo 8 Creativity 8 People 9 total 8', '2002-05-28 16:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64473, 1819, 1175, '<td valign="top">I''m gonna guess that you didn''t know them and so you had to probably keep a safe distance.  You could have had a GREAT photo if you just had a telephoto lens and focused on a couple of guys around the ball.  Besides that the picture is a bit dark fora  bright day on the beach.</td>', 'I''m gonna guess that you didn''t know them and so you had to probably keep a safe distance.  You could have had a GREAT photo if you just had a telephoto lens and focused on a couple of guys around the ball.  Besides that the picture is a bit dark fora  bright day on the beach.', '2002-05-28 16:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64474, 1819, 811, '<td valign="top">The people in the foreground take away from the boys.  Getting closer (I know it may not have been possible) to the group, or focusing on one of the closer ones may have been more effective.</td>', 'The people in the foreground take away from the boys.  Getting closer (I know it may not have been possible) to the group, or focusing on one of the closer ones may have been more effective.', '2002-05-28 16:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64475, 1819, 689, '<td valign="top">A little too far away ...</td>', 'A little too far away ...', '2002-05-28 18:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64476, 1819, 1599, '<td valign="top">cool</td>', 'cool', '2002-05-29 16:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64477, 1819, 1379, '<td valign="top">Nice how you caught those guys so evenly spaced.  I wish this had a less washed-out look, though.</td>', 'Nice how you caught those guys so evenly spaced.  I wish this had a less washed-out look, though.', '2002-05-29 17:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64478, 1819, 1679, '<td valign="top">Underexposed.....<br/>Horizon is also not level. That''s a pity. It would have made a nice shot.<br/>Errrrm, where is the sun?</td>', 'Underexposed.....Horizon is also not level. That''s a pity. It would have made a nice shot.Errrrm, where is the sun?', '2002-05-29 18:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64479, 1819, 2, '<td valign="top">I''d like this picture better without the people in the foreground, though I''m sure that was hard to do.  The guys themselves, though, seem off-center.</td>', 'I''d like this picture better without the people in the foreground, though I''m sure that was hard to do.  The guys themselves, though, seem off-center.', '2002-05-30 20:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64480, 1819, 1, '<td valign="top">This photo could''ve been SO much stronger could you have cropped out the people in the front.  move to the left and zoom in a bit.  With all th foreground mess it seems very poorly composed.</td>', 'This photo could''ve been SO much stronger could you have cropped out the people in the front.  move to the left and zoom in a bit.  With all th foreground mess it seems very poorly composed.', '2002-05-30 22:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64481, 1819, 1037, '<td valign="top">I like the way the guys are silhouetted against the water. A bit of post processing would have made this photo a lot cooler.</td>', 'I like the way the guys are silhouetted against the water. A bit of post processing would have made this photo a lot cooler.', '2002-05-31 03:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64482, 1819, 1078, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, but I think it would have been even better as a photo if you''d moved closer to the main subjects so you could avoid placing all the other people in the foreground.  I didn''t realize at first, but the actual horizon (the ocean) is crooked, while the perceptual horizon is straight.  It didn''t bother me until I realized it, but it''s not very noticeable.  I like the idea of these guys as silhouettes, but I''m not sure if you''d be able to tell what they''re doing if you went that far.  Maybe if you just brought up the levels over all -- the sand and ocean are pretty dark.</td>', 'Nice idea, but I think it would have been even better as a photo if you''d moved closer to the main subjects so you could avoid placing all the other people in the foreground.  I didn''t realize at first, but the actual horizon (the ocean) is crooked, while the perceptual horizon is straight.  It didn''t bother me until I realized it, but it''s not very noticeable.  I like the idea of these guys as silhouettes, but I''m not sure if you''d be able to tell what they''re doing if you went that far.  Maybe if you just brought up the levels over all -- the sand and ocean are pretty dark.', '2002-05-31 12:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64490, 1826, 668, '<td valign="top">we are energy.  recycled and re-usable   <br/>i like</td>', 'we are energy.  recycled and re-usable   i like', '2002-05-27 11:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64491, 1826, 1175, '<td valign="top">Did you miss the advertisement challenge from a few weeks ago?  This weeks challenge is People, and I don''t see any in your picture.</td>', 'Did you miss the advertisement challenge from a few weeks ago?  This weeks challenge is People, and I don''t see any in your picture.', '2002-05-27 11:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64492, 1826, 772, '<td valign="top">I don''t see any interpretation of a PEOPLE theme with this photo... Maybe this would have worked as an advertisement challenge....</td>', 'I don''t see any interpretation of a PEOPLE theme with this photo... Maybe this would have worked as an advertisement challenge....', '2002-05-27 01:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64493, 1826, 1037, '<td valign="top">A friend of mine explained the reference to "The Matrix" to me, otherwise I would never have gotten this photo. I''ve only seen about half of that movie, and it was just a hollywood imitation of something far more interesting. I understand how that context makes this a photo about ''people'' in a clever kind of way, and that hand is really well lit, but it''s a bit obscure and seems about as shallow in a pretentious kind of way as the movie did. (Oops, getting a bit nasty... hmm, oh well). Still, I can''t rate it low.</td>', 'A friend of mine explained the reference to "The Matrix" to me, otherwise I would never have gotten this photo. I''ve only seen about half of that movie, and it was just a hollywood imitation of something far more interesting. I understand how that context makes this a photo about ''people'' in a clever kind of way, and that hand is really well lit, but it''s a bit obscure and seems about as shallow in a pretentious kind of way as the movie did. (Oops, getting a bit nasty... hmm, oh well). Still, I can''t rate it low.', '2002-05-27 03:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64494, 1826, 689, '<td valign="top">Where are the people?</td>', 'Where are the people?', '2002-05-27 06:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64495, 1826, 509, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting effect around your hand.  Without it, this shot wouldn''t be that interesting, but it brings the hand and the battery into a stronger focus.  How did you do that?  Nice play on the challenge topic</td>', 'I like the lighting effect around your hand.  Without it, this shot wouldn''t be that interesting, but it brings the hand and the battery into a stronger focus.  How did you do that?  Nice play on the challenge topic', '2002-05-27 08:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
