(64738, 1846, 885, '<td valign="top">Looks like a cover of an album.  What is it taken through?  The white balance is obviously off, but it does give a certain mood, and the contrast is way up.  I don''t mind the undetailed shadows as much as that blown out white something on the right side of the frame.</td>', 'Looks like a cover of an album.  What is it taken through?  The white balance is obviously off, but it does give a certain mood, and the contrast is way up.  I don''t mind the undetailed shadows as much as that blown out white something on the right side of the frame.', '2002-05-29 14:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64739, 1846, 1, '<td valign="top">The fish-eye effect used is cool I guess, but now with the black borders.  I can''t imagine that a lens did this -- it looks like a mirror.  I''d suggested getting an actual fish-eye lens.  Also your tones seem washde out, I think of better source of lighting would''ve allowed more options.</td>', 'The fish-eye effect used is cool I guess, but now with the black borders.  I can''t imagine that a lens did this -- it looks like a mirror.  I''d suggested getting an actual fish-eye lens.  Also your tones seem washde out, I think of better source of lighting would''ve allowed more options.', '2002-05-29 06:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64740, 1846, 1005, '<td valign="top">Nice fisheye effect.  A few little nits:  Window behind lead guitar way tooo harsh; somewhat yellow tint all over; poor light on both guitarists; maybe guitarists are a bit too close to the edge (notice the lead guitar''s head is missing, is that a Les Paul?); misc. grip about the framing, but there''s really nothing you could do about it.<br/>Photo 9 Creativity 10 ++ People 10 (although I really, really like this shot, I have to give the final score -1 because of downsides to the additional lens, sorry)  total 9</td>', 'Nice fisheye effect.  A few little nits:  Window behind lead guitar way tooo harsh; somewhat yellow tint all over; poor light on both guitarists; maybe guitarists are a bit too close to the edge (notice the lead guitar''s head is missing, is that a Les Paul?); misc. grip about the framing, but there''s really nothing you could do about it.Photo 9 Creativity 10 ++ People 10 (although I really, really like this shot, I have to give the final score -1 because of downsides to the additional lens, sorry)  total 9', '2002-05-29 17:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
