(64904, 1858, 741, '<td valign="top">Excellent!  If your camera allows this I would have been tempted to open up the aperture (smaller F stop) to reduce the depth of field so that the dog was still sharp and the guy was slightly less in focus - at the moment he''s so sharp he''s distracting from the action (mind you, if you''d done this you would have got comments about it not being a people shot!).  Assuming it wasn''t me taking this shot - I''d suggest getting lower down so that the dog really is right on top of you.</td>', 'Excellent!  If your camera allows this I would have been tempted to open up the aperture (smaller F stop) to reduce the depth of field so that the dog was still sharp and the guy was slightly less in focus - at the moment he''s so sharp he''s distracting from the action (mind you, if you''d done this you would have got comments about it not being a people shot!).  Assuming it wasn''t me taking this shot - I''d suggest getting lower down so that the dog really is right on top of you.', '2002-05-28 00:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
