(64948, 1860, 1903, '<td valign="top">I like the simplicity of this photo.</td>', 'I like the simplicity of this photo.', '2002-05-29 15:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64949, 1860, 885, '<td valign="top">Pretty repetition of those purple doors.  Interesting subject, too.  If it were my photo, I think I might have been tempted to try cropping way down to eliminate the non-purple doors on the right, which would make the subject a little more off-center, I think.  Also, the fact that the door isn''t parallel with the edge of the frame bothers me a bit.</td>', 'Pretty repetition of those purple doors.  Interesting subject, too.  If it were my photo, I think I might have been tempted to try cropping way down to eliminate the non-purple doors on the right, which would make the subject a little more off-center, I think.  Also, the fact that the door isn''t parallel with the edge of the frame bothers me a bit.', '2002-05-30 08:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64950, 1860, 1175, '<td valign="top">its funny... one of the things I read was that the subject should fill the frame, but I kind of enjoy him actually being small.  .with no one around himit gives you the impression that he''s alone.</td>', 'its funny... one of the things I read was that the subject should fill the frame, but I kind of enjoy him actually being small.  .with no one around himit gives you the impression that he''s alone.', '2002-05-30 20:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64951, 1860, 1, '<td valign="top">Nicely caught, I like the framing a lot even though it''s a wide angle.  The colors work great too (brown/purple).  I think maybe if you zoomed in or cropped off the blue doors at the end it''d look even better -- just the 3 purple doors.</td>', 'Nicely caught, I like the framing a lot even though it''s a wide angle.  The colors work great too (brown/purple).  I think maybe if you zoomed in or cropped off the blue doors at the end it''d look even better -- just the 3 purple doors.', '2002-05-30 21:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(64952, 1860, 811, '<td valign="top">I like the left to right moving feel this picture has -- good use of diagonal lines.  If it had been possible to get him more in the left side of the picture, or been closer to him, that may have made a neat shot as well.</td>', 'I like the left to right moving feel this picture has -- good use of diagonal lines.  If it had been possible to get him more in the left side of the picture, or been closer to him, that may have made a neat shot as well.', '2002-05-31 12:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
